WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.160
The O R W base includes shared busbar geometry and electrical requirements

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:05.080
for I T equipment.

3
00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:08.660
Use those interfaces to connect the frame review to the actual power

4
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:12.620
path, while retaining implementation-specific capacity and operating conditions.

5
00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:17.420
The animation reveals the rack boundaries and a short requirement-level power-entry sequence.

6
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.080
The equipment's power-entry control prevents powering before the input connector is fully

7
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:25.880
asserted and turns it off before removal, as described in the specification.

8
00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:30.600
It doesn't invent contact timing, an internal precharge circuit or a live-service

9
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:31.040
procedure.

10
00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.080
Cooling needs its own evidence.

11
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:38.260
Identify the manifolds, couplings, equipment interfaces and receiving loop in the selected

12
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.000
implementation.

13
00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:43.940
A shared mechanical frame doesn't guarantee common fluid conditions or thermal performance.

14
00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:48.180
Attach the electrical and thermal records to the same configured system used

15
00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:49.040
in the payload review.

16
00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:52.940
This is how the wider frame becomes an integrated rack decision rather

17
00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.300
than a mechanical approval with unexamined subsystems added afterward.

